WEBVTT

1
00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:46.296
Shit. shit. shit.

2
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:47.589
Whoa.

3
00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:15.367
Excuse me. sir. You have to help me.
My grandmother. she's hurt.

4
00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.869
- Try to stay calm.
- No. I can't lose her.

5
00:01:16.952 --> 00:01:19.496
We're gonna take care of your grandmother.
but we need to get you on a stretcher too.

6
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.957
I'm fine. I just...
I need to be with her.

7
00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.376
You're still in shock.
You could have serious injuries.

8
00:01:26.003 --> 00:01:29.673
Sir. please let me go with her.
If she dies. and I'm not with her...

9
00:01:30.424 --> 00:01:31.800
Please.

10
00:01:33.719 --> 00:01:34.761
- Okay.
- Thank you.

11
00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:58.785
Seventy-one year old woman.
multiple injuries.

12
00:01:58.869 --> 00:02:01.079
Possible head trauma. collapsed lung.

13
00:02:01.163 --> 00:02:03.957
Blood pressure around 50.
We got it up to 80 with adrenaline.

14
00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.294
It's okay.
Can you squeeze my hand?

15
00:02:09.213 --> 00:02:10.506
Can you try to squeeze it?

16
00:02:16.386 --> 00:02:18.597
Hey! Excuse me. You're the granddaughter?

17
00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.933
Uh. what? Um. yes.

18
00:02:21.016 --> 00:02:22.476
And what's her name?

19
00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:24.436
- Ruth Turner.
- And you are?

20
00:02:25.229 --> 00:02:28.524
- Amanda... Turner.
- Okay.

21
00:02:28.607 --> 00:02:30.526
Is she on any current medications?

22
00:02:30.609 --> 00:02:32.778
I'm not sure.

23
00:02:32.861 --> 00:02:34.863
Can you help
with her medical history?

24
00:02:35.948 --> 00:02:39.201
- No. I... No.
- Any preexisting conditions?

25
00:02:39.284 --> 00:02:41.286
I was just visiting her for the week.
okay? I don't...

26
00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:42.871
Is she gonna be okay?

27
00:02:42.955 --> 00:02:44.164
We'll do our best to save her.

28
00:02:44.748 --> 00:02:45.749
Okay.

29
00:02:51.797 --> 00:02:54.216
- Hey. we need to get you checked out too.
- No. I'm fine.

30
00:02:55.217 --> 00:02:57.928
- You're in shock.
- I'm fine.

31
00:02:59.263 --> 00:03:01.890
Is there a drinking fountain?
I just really need some water.

32
00:03:01.974 --> 00:03:04.643
I'll get you a cup.
Stay right there. I'll be right back.

33
00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:17.155
No!

34
00:03:17.239 --> 00:03:18.574
- Faster. Lucky. Come on.
- I'm trying.

35
00:03:22.786 --> 00:03:24.037
Are you okay?

36
00:05:19.069 --> 00:05:20.404
Feeling better?

37
00:05:20.487 --> 00:05:21.488
Um...

38
00:05:24.074 --> 00:05:26.285
- How long have I been here?
- Not long.

39
00:05:27.119 --> 00:05:28.996
- What happened?
- You fainted.

40
00:05:29.079 --> 00:05:31.081
It's pretty common
in situations like yours.

41
00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:32.833
You were running on adrenaline.

42
00:05:32.916 --> 00:05:34.293
Ruth is in surgery.

43
00:05:34.376 --> 00:05:35.377
Who?

44
00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:36.461
Your grandmother.

45
00:05:37.671 --> 00:05:40.299
She's still critical.
but they're doing everything they can.

46
00:05:40.382 --> 00:05:41.675
You rest. okay?

47
00:05:56.565 --> 00:05:58.192
Oh. my God. Billie.

48
00:06:03.989 --> 00:06:05.782
Hey. She's going to be okay.

49
00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:32.851
Here.

50
00:06:33.477 --> 00:06:34.478
I'm fine.

51
00:06:35.812 --> 00:06:36.855
You don't look fine.

52
00:06:43.111 --> 00:06:45.614
Someone I love might die.

53
00:06:45.697 --> 00:06:48.075
And the last thing I said to her was.
"I hate you."

54
00:06:52.037 --> 00:06:54.373
I used to tell my dad
I hated him all the time.

55
00:06:55.832 --> 00:06:56.834
Didn't mean it.

56
00:06:59.002 --> 00:07:01.839
I would've done anything for him.
and I think he knew that.

57
00:07:06.218 --> 00:07:07.511
Maybe that's what I hated.

58
00:07:08.095 --> 00:07:09.388
I don't know what to do.

59
00:07:12.641 --> 00:07:15.352
Go in there and make sure she knows
you didn't mean it.

60
00:08:22.711 --> 00:08:24.213
Oh. Are you okay?

61
00:08:25.422 --> 00:08:26.423
Yeah.

62
00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:31.345
I'm fine. I just. uh. need a room
for the night. Whatever's cheapest.

63
00:08:32.304 --> 00:08:33.597
Of course. ID. please.

64
00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:34.681
Yeah.

65
00:08:49.863 --> 00:08:53.116
Hello. I'm Peter Kershaw. Billie's boss.

66
00:08:53.617 --> 00:08:56.245
Yeah. I'm Alison. We've met before.

67
00:08:56.328 --> 00:08:57.746
Uh. uh...

68
00:08:59.373 --> 00:09:01.208
How's. uh... How's she doing?

69
00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:04.169
She has a cranial contusion.

70
00:09:04.962 --> 00:09:07.714
They're gonna keep her a couple of days
for observation.

71
00:09:07.798 --> 00:09:09.967
You catch the people she was after?

72
00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:12.803
One of them was dead on arrival.
We're still looking for the other one.

73
00:09:12.886 --> 00:09:14.805
Who? Who's dead?

74
00:09:15.472 --> 00:09:18.350
Cary Masterson. Gunshot wound.

75
00:09:19.142 --> 00:09:21.270
- And Lucky?
- We don't have her.

76
00:09:24.064 --> 00:09:25.983
Then. what are you doing here?

77
00:09:26.567 --> 00:09:28.694
Just making sure
you didn't get yourself killed.

78
00:09:30.195 --> 00:09:33.365
Let me have some water.

79
00:09:33.448 --> 00:09:36.243
I'm sure she's not far.

80
00:09:36.326 --> 00:09:39.788
She's probably hurt somewhere.
You need to find her while she's local.

81
00:09:39.872 --> 00:09:42.749
Yeah. And you need to stop obsessing
and get some rest.

82
00:09:42.833 --> 00:09:43.792
Amen.

83
00:09:45.002 --> 00:09:46.670
- Where's Gates?
- Doing his job.

84
00:09:46.753 --> 00:09:48.463
That's your last question. all right?

85
00:09:48.547 --> 00:09:50.966
I came here to check on you.
not rile you up.

86
00:09:51.592 --> 00:09:54.011
All right? I'll let you know
when we have any updates.

87
00:10:05.314 --> 00:10:06.440
Here you go.

88
00:10:17.409 --> 00:10:19.411
I. uh... I want him cremated.

89
00:10:21.413 --> 00:10:24.958
And we'll do a memorial service
as soon as possible.

90
00:10:28.045 --> 00:10:31.507
I don't want him lying alone
in some cold. dark morgue.

91
00:10:33.091 --> 00:10:34.384
I'll take care of it.

92
00:10:35.928 --> 00:10:37.596
I don't know who his friends are.

93
00:10:39.097 --> 00:10:40.516
Or even if he has any.

94
00:10:40.599 --> 00:10:44.853
I guess it will be my people.

95
00:10:48.065 --> 00:10:50.442
I suppose I don't have many
of those left either.

96
00:10:51.735 --> 00:10:52.903
More than you think.

97
00:10:57.199 --> 00:10:58.534
Wayne should be told.

98
00:10:59.993 --> 00:11:01.411
I'll call his people.

99
00:11:06.124 --> 00:11:07.292
You think he'll come?

100
00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:13.841
Hmm.

101
00:11:14.675 --> 00:11:16.927
Let's put the boy to rest. Set him free.

102
00:11:18.387 --> 00:11:19.388
Hmm.

103
00:11:19.471 --> 00:11:22.808
Everything else is. um...
Well. it's just secondary.

104
00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:27.437
Yeah. you're right.

105
00:11:30.524 --> 00:11:32.109
I'm gonna give you some space.

106
00:11:32.693 --> 00:11:34.695
You can sit down. Please.

107
00:11:37.531 --> 00:11:39.366
Go ahead. you can call them now.

108
00:11:40.826 --> 00:11:42.411
See what Wayne has to say.

109
00:12:20.991 --> 00:12:23.744
<i>It's nothing.
I don't know what I'm trying to say.</i>

110
00:12:24.411 --> 00:12:25.412
I think you do.

111
00:12:26.663 --> 00:12:28.248
Are we bad people?

112
00:12:29.333 --> 00:12:30.667
What makes you think that?

113
00:12:32.711 --> 00:12:34.671
Well. I'm pretty sure
we're not good people.

114
00:12:36.965 --> 00:12:38.592
Given it a lot of thought. huh?

115
00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:44.848
What's our source of heat? On Earth.

116
00:12:45.766 --> 00:12:46.934
The sun.

117
00:12:47.017 --> 00:12:48.310
What's our source of cold?

118
00:12:52.606 --> 00:12:53.774
Antarctica?

119
00:12:54.358 --> 00:12:55.692
There is no source of cold.

120
00:12:56.652 --> 00:12:58.362
Cold is just the absence of heat.

121
00:12:58.862 --> 00:13:02.574
So it just becomes a question
of how far you are from the sun.

122
00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:05.035
Mmm. it's a question of degree.

123
00:13:06.828 --> 00:13:10.165
So you're saying there is no evil?
Just how far you are from good?

124
00:13:11.333 --> 00:13:13.627
Good and evil are man-made concepts.

125
00:13:14.628 --> 00:13:17.631
And like everything else man-made.
they're highly imperfect.

126
00:13:17.714 --> 00:13:19.466
Do you think a lion wastes one second

127
00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:22.052
wondering whether it's good or bad
to kill an antelope?

128
00:13:22.135 --> 00:13:24.680
He's doing what he has to to survive.

129
00:13:24.763 --> 00:13:26.932
Yeah. but we're not animals.

130
00:13:27.015 --> 00:13:28.809
Only because we say we're not.

131
00:14:59.191 --> 00:15:00.943
What can I get you?

132
00:15:01.026 --> 00:15:04.780
Your cheapest bourbon. please.
and a sugar cube.

133
00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:14.831
It's on the house.

134
00:15:17.376 --> 00:15:18.627
Thank you.

135
00:15:24.591 --> 00:15:28.387
Isn't that some shit?
Some people have all the luck.

136
00:15:29.805 --> 00:15:32.724
You'll have to excuse me.
You caught me in a bad mood.

137
00:15:34.309 --> 00:15:35.310
It's all right.

138
00:15:35.394 --> 00:15:37.771
My flight home got canceled.

139
00:15:40.107 --> 00:15:42.234
I've had a pretty shitty day myself. so...

140
00:15:44.403 --> 00:15:47.322
Well then. to our bad luck.

141
00:15:52.911 --> 00:15:54.913
- And fuck that guy.
- Yeah.

142
00:15:54.997 --> 00:15:55.998
Fuck that guy.

143
00:15:58.876 --> 00:16:01.295
Now I'm missing my daughter's birthday
because of that flight.

144
00:16:01.378 --> 00:16:03.380
I just don't wanna fuck her up. you know?

145
00:16:05.591 --> 00:16:07.509
The fact that you're worried about that

146
00:16:07.593 --> 00:16:09.803
probably means that
you have nothing to worry about.

147
00:16:16.435 --> 00:16:17.769
So. what happened to you?

148
00:16:19.146 --> 00:16:22.608
The. um. bellman gave me
the wrong suitcase.

149
00:16:23.984 --> 00:16:26.695
Which means that somebody's
probably out there with mine.

150
00:16:27.654 --> 00:16:31.658
They promised me they're gonna
track it down. but until then. I'm...

151
00:16:31.742 --> 00:16:34.536
You're just wearing
some stranger's clothes?

152
00:16:39.875 --> 00:16:41.126
No.

153
00:16:43.795 --> 00:16:46.548
No. these are my husband's clothes.
actually. He. uh...

154
00:16:50.302 --> 00:16:51.512
He died today.

155
00:16:57.976 --> 00:17:01.063
I'm wearing them because
mine are covered in blood.

156
00:17:01.146 --> 00:17:03.857
We were in a car wreck. and now he's dead.

157
00:17:03.941 --> 00:17:06.984
And I'm here talking to you.

158
00:17:10.614 --> 00:17:14.201
Sorry. you'll have to. uh. forgive me.
I'm not very used to being honest.

159
00:17:15.536 --> 00:17:19.080
Uh. any other day. I would've
just continued the bullshit suitcase story

160
00:17:19.164 --> 00:17:24.252
and used your guilt over your daughter
to manipulate you into paying for my room

161
00:17:24.336 --> 00:17:26.003
and giving me some extra money...

162
00:17:28.131 --> 00:17:30.509
And you know what's really shitty
about all of that?

163
00:17:30.592 --> 00:17:32.469
Is that I wouldn't even
have to ask you for it.

164
00:17:32.553 --> 00:17:35.347
You would insist.

165
00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:37.683
Because I know the perfect words to use

166
00:17:37.766 --> 00:17:39.852
for a guy who worries
about his little girl.

167
00:17:44.731 --> 00:17:46.066
But that's not what you're doing?

168
00:17:51.405 --> 00:17:53.949
No.

169
00:17:56.577 --> 00:17:57.703
Why not?

170
00:17:59.621 --> 00:18:01.748
Because I'm really tired
of being this way.

171
00:18:03.333 --> 00:18:04.418
And. um...

172
00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:10.299
today I really need to believe
that I'm not a totally bad person.

173
00:18:20.893 --> 00:18:23.687
Well. someone wise once told me.

174
00:18:25.314 --> 00:18:26.940
"The fact that you're worried about it

175
00:18:27.024 --> 00:18:28.734
probably means
you don't have to worry about it."

176
00:18:32.863 --> 00:18:34.114
She wasn't very wise.

177
00:18:42.623 --> 00:18:44.708
The car wreck. your husband.

178
00:18:47.252 --> 00:18:48.504
That's true?

179
00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:55.010
We were fighting.

180
00:18:57.471 --> 00:18:59.139
And I really regret what I said.

181
00:19:09.107 --> 00:19:11.109
Those don't have to be your last words.

182
00:19:17.157 --> 00:19:18.325
Okay. Yoda.

183
00:19:24.164 --> 00:19:25.791
- Thanks.
- Want another drink?

184
00:19:25.874 --> 00:19:27.501
- Yeah. Yeah.
- Yeah?

185
00:19:27.584 --> 00:19:30.128
Can we get another one. please?

186
00:19:35.759 --> 00:19:37.177
Oh. fuck. Priscilla.

187
00:19:40.806 --> 00:19:41.890
Priscilla!

188
00:19:42.933 --> 00:19:44.059
Priscilla.

189
00:20:02.411 --> 00:20:04.872
Oh. it feels so good.

190
00:20:09.793 --> 00:20:11.086
Oh.

191
00:20:40.407 --> 00:20:44.828
Did I kill him. Dutch?
Did I do this?

192
00:20:45.746 --> 00:20:48.582
- Of course not.
- No. Did I put him in that car?

193
00:20:49.541 --> 00:20:53.504
If he would have done what you told him
to do. he'd... he'd be alive right now.

194
00:20:53.587 --> 00:20:55.547
Yeah. but I... I put him in the life.

195
00:20:55.631 --> 00:20:57.424
- I pushed him too hard.
- Come on.

196
00:20:57.508 --> 00:20:59.051
No good's gonna come out
of talking like this.

197
00:20:59.134 --> 00:21:01.887
Yes. but I did... I did though.
I mean. I could have...

198
00:21:02.804 --> 00:21:05.098
I could have sent him away
to boarding school.

199
00:21:05.599 --> 00:21:07.768
I could have done better by him.

200
00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:13.941
I mean. it's normal in bad moments to...
to look back and do a...

201
00:21:14.024 --> 00:21:16.151
a warped accounting of sorts. you know?

202
00:21:18.028 --> 00:21:20.197
You might wanna find
somebody to blame even...

203
00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:21.740
you know. even if it's ourselves.

204
00:21:21.823 --> 00:21:23.742
That's just not how life works
in real-time. you know?

205
00:21:23.825 --> 00:21:27.704
Life is just a million random choices
you make day after day. year after year.

206
00:21:27.788 --> 00:21:29.873
and later on. you can. uh...

207
00:21:29.957 --> 00:21:32.417
you know. manipulate them
to add up to anything you want.

208
00:21:32.501 --> 00:21:35.796
- But... that doesn't make it true.
- Hmm.

209
00:21:38.507 --> 00:21:41.677
Yeah. I don't know if you're being wise
or just full of shit.

210
00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:44.930
It's a fine line.

211
00:21:48.892 --> 00:21:51.770
You. uh... You gonna be...

212
00:21:51.854 --> 00:21:54.231
shooting my piece any more there?

213
00:21:54.314 --> 00:21:56.859
Uh... not right now.

214
00:21:56.942 --> 00:21:58.610
Okay. 'cause I gotta reload it.

215
00:21:59.945 --> 00:22:00.988
Oh.

216
00:22:09.705 --> 00:22:11.373
They're discharging you already?

217
00:22:11.456 --> 00:22:13.292
More like she's discharging herself.

218
00:22:13.375 --> 00:22:14.626
The doctor said I could go.

219
00:22:14.710 --> 00:22:17.212
No. What he said is
he couldn't force you to stay.

220
00:22:17.796 --> 00:22:19.298
Mmm. That's it. babe.

221
00:22:19.381 --> 00:22:21.425
I'll meet you two down in the car.

222
00:22:26.847 --> 00:22:29.725
- You need to take it easy.
- I'll try to do that.

223
00:22:29.808 --> 00:22:30.809
Will you?

224
00:22:31.685 --> 00:22:35.189
We lost all our leads.

225
00:22:35.272 --> 00:22:38.483
No Cary. No money. No Lucky.

226
00:22:38.567 --> 00:22:40.819
We will find something again.
We always do.

227
00:22:40.903 --> 00:22:42.279
Not by taking it easy.

228
00:24:20.210 --> 00:24:22.963
Priscilla. I am so sorry.

229
00:24:25.340 --> 00:24:26.592
Priscilla.

230
00:24:27.634 --> 00:24:28.844
Mmm...

231
00:24:42.482 --> 00:24:47.029
So. uh. did he even bother
to send flowers?

232
00:24:48.405 --> 00:24:50.490
Flowers wouldn't have made a difference.

233
00:25:02.503 --> 00:25:04.004
Uh. wh-where are you going?

234
00:25:05.297 --> 00:25:06.965
I need to be alone.

235
00:25:07.049 --> 00:25:08.967
You have a lot of people here.

236
00:25:09.051 --> 00:25:10.344
That's why I'm leaving.

237
00:25:43.168 --> 00:25:44.169
Priscilla.

238
00:25:45.963 --> 00:25:47.673
There's someone here to see you.

239
00:25:54.429 --> 00:25:55.597
I'll leave you two be.

240
00:26:02.062 --> 00:26:03.981
You got some nerve showing up here.

241
00:26:05.399 --> 00:26:06.859
He was my husband.

242
00:26:06.942 --> 00:26:09.987
Yeah. well.
he was always a bit too easily led.

243
00:26:11.280 --> 00:26:13.365
Yeah. Till he wasn't.

244
00:26:13.949 --> 00:26:15.242
Until he wasn't.

245
00:26:16.910 --> 00:26:18.537
Why are you here. Lucky?

246
00:26:19.705 --> 00:26:20.873
The money is gone.

247
00:26:22.374 --> 00:26:23.876
What do you mean "gone"?

248
00:26:23.959 --> 00:26:26.170
Cary was the only person
who knew where it was.

249
00:26:26.253 --> 00:26:28.797
Uh-huh. And he didn't tell you.

250
00:26:28.881 --> 00:26:30.215
Never got the chance.

251
00:26:31.383 --> 00:26:32.843
You expect me to believe that?

252
00:26:32.926 --> 00:26:35.179
You're gonna believe
whatever you want to believe.

253
00:26:36.471 --> 00:26:37.472
Did you love him?

254
00:26:42.227 --> 00:26:43.312
I did.

255
00:26:46.690 --> 00:26:48.192
More than you will ever know.

256
00:26:48.775 --> 00:26:49.860
How touching.

257
00:26:51.904 --> 00:26:53.864
Priscilla. I can't keep running from you.

258
00:26:53.947 --> 00:26:56.283
I gave you and John the opportunity

259
00:26:56.366 --> 00:26:59.369
to rise above
his little nickel-and-dime schemes.

260
00:27:00.037 --> 00:27:02.289
I saw real potential in you.
You fucked me.

261
00:27:02.372 --> 00:27:05.584
Potential? We were pawns to you. Always.

262
00:27:06.502 --> 00:27:08.879
Well. that's how you get in.
You pay your dues.

263
00:27:08.962 --> 00:27:13.300
John never did a single damn thing
he didn't wanna do.

264
00:27:13.383 --> 00:27:14.635
He knew the score.

265
00:27:14.718 --> 00:27:18.972
Just like he knew what would happen to him
if he stole from me.

266
00:27:20.557 --> 00:27:23.227
Okay. So. what now?

267
00:27:24.603 --> 00:27:28.315
Well. now I'm gonna go upstairs
and grieve my son.

268
00:27:28.398 --> 00:27:30.651
and you're gonna get the hell
off my beach.

269
00:27:31.318 --> 00:27:34.947
And I suggest you figure out a way
to get your hands on that money.

270
00:27:35.030 --> 00:27:38.116
because the next time I see you.
I won't be so goddamn cordial.

271
00:28:09.815 --> 00:28:11.817
I hate you!

272
00:28:19.491 --> 00:28:22.202
<i>Apple. hamster. karma.</i>

273
00:28:22.286 --> 00:28:27.457
<i>snow. holiday. sunset. pledge.</i>

274
00:28:27.541 --> 00:28:33.088
<i>turkey. identity. purpose.
fossil. mushroom.</i>

275
00:28:43.015 --> 00:28:45.517
<i>Apple. hamster. karma...</i>

276
00:28:45.601 --> 00:28:51.273
<i>snow. holiday. sunset. pledge. turkey...</i>

277
00:28:51.356 --> 00:28:53.942
<i>identity. purpose.</i>

278
00:28:54.026 --> 00:28:56.236
<i>fossil. mushroom.</i>

279
00:29:05.370 --> 00:29:08.248
Yes!

280
00:29:26.600 --> 00:29:27.851
Okay...

281
00:29:31.188 --> 00:29:33.232
You know they gave you muscle relaxers.

282
00:29:33.315 --> 00:29:36.818
Those things make me groggy.

283
00:29:36.902 --> 00:29:38.946
Maybe you need to be groggy.

284
00:29:40.072 --> 00:29:41.740
Hand me my laptop. please.

285
00:29:41.823 --> 00:29:43.325
The doctor said no screen time.

286
00:29:45.744 --> 00:29:47.788
You know I relax when I work.

287
00:29:48.539 --> 00:29:53.418
And the doctor said minimize screen time.
I'm "minimizing."

288
00:29:53.502 --> 00:29:55.170
Wow.

289
00:29:55.254 --> 00:29:58.298
So now you're making me your enabler
and your drug dealer.

290
00:29:58.382 --> 00:29:59.716
It's Advil. girl.

291
00:30:03.053 --> 00:30:04.054
Thank you.

292
00:30:05.889 --> 00:30:06.890
Oh. God.

293
00:30:08.767 --> 00:30:14.356
Here. Sit next to me.
We can cowork-relax together.

294
00:30:14.439 --> 00:30:16.900
That's not a thing. That's weird.

295
00:30:16.984 --> 00:30:19.361
- You calling me weird?
- You're weird. Yes.

296
00:30:19.444 --> 00:30:22.114
Calling me weird.

297
00:30:23.073 --> 00:30:27.035
What's more relaxing than going over
the details of a three-year-old case? Huh?

298
00:30:27.119 --> 00:30:30.747
- What's more relaxing than that?
- I don't know. an edible.

299
00:30:31.832 --> 00:30:33.333
That's not funny.

300
00:30:33.417 --> 00:30:35.544
- And I'm gonna call the DEA on you.
- Okay.

301
00:30:35.627 --> 00:30:36.753
Okay.

302
00:30:37.713 --> 00:30:38.714
An edible.

303
00:30:39.423 --> 00:30:41.466
- Wait. wait. Go back.
- What?

304
00:30:42.050 --> 00:30:43.635
Go back. That woman.

305
00:30:47.890 --> 00:30:49.474
I think I saw her.

306
00:30:50.601 --> 00:30:51.852
You saw this woman?

307
00:30:52.686 --> 00:30:56.899
Yeah. at the hospital.
The day of the crash. In the bathroom.

308
00:30:59.610 --> 00:31:00.777
What was she doing?

309
00:31:02.529 --> 00:31:04.281
- I don't remember.
- Dana.

310
00:31:04.364 --> 00:31:08.869
Dana. honey. I need you to remember.
What was she doing?

311
00:31:08.952 --> 00:31:10.871
Jesus. Mom. I don't know.

312
00:31:11.747 --> 00:31:14.791
She was washing blood off her arm
or something.

313
00:31:14.875 --> 00:31:16.251
Did she talk to you?

314
00:31:17.461 --> 00:31:18.962
She talked about her dad.

315
00:31:19.630 --> 00:31:20.714
Okay. What about him?

316
00:31:21.632 --> 00:31:24.927
Something about how she hated
that she would do anything for him.

317
00:31:29.473 --> 00:31:31.308
Mom?

318
00:31:31.391 --> 00:31:34.102
- Where's my phone?
- Why?

319
00:31:34.186 --> 00:31:36.730
- Wh... You're not supposed to be working.
- Where's my phone?

320
00:31:36.813 --> 00:31:39.316
- Mom. you're not...
- It's behind you.

321
00:31:41.193 --> 00:31:42.736
- Mom.
- It's fine.

322
00:31:46.281 --> 00:31:48.242
Gates.

323
00:31:50.452 --> 00:31:52.996
Yeah. I need you to call a favor in
to the DOJ...

324
00:31:53.080 --> 00:31:54.122
<i>Yes. ma'am.</i>

325
00:31:54.206 --> 00:31:56.708
But this stays between me. you.
and the wall.

326
00:32:35.956 --> 00:32:37.457
You have an update for me?

327
00:32:42.671 --> 00:32:43.672
Fuck you.

328
00:32:44.590 --> 00:32:46.091
So. that's a no?

329
00:32:48.051 --> 00:32:50.387
You know. I never asked you
for child support.

330
00:32:51.263 --> 00:32:55.726
I never asked you to be a father.
I never asked anything of you.

331
00:32:55.809 --> 00:32:57.144
You were well compensated.

332
00:33:04.359 --> 00:33:07.237
- Get out. Get out.
- He was your son.

333
00:33:07.321 --> 00:33:09.198
You couldn't show one shred
of human decency?

334
00:33:09.281 --> 00:33:11.283
- Get out!
- Our son is dead.

335
00:33:11.366 --> 00:33:12.910
He was already dead.

336
00:33:12.993 --> 00:33:15.162
He was dead
the minute he stole that money.

337
00:33:15.245 --> 00:33:18.582
Did you really think that I was just
gonna let him walk away from this?

338
00:33:18.665 --> 00:33:20.834
And if you knew what was good for you.
you'd be out there.

339
00:33:20.918 --> 00:33:24.505
and you'd be looking for it instead
of throwing your little fucking tantrums.

340
00:33:25.672 --> 00:33:27.216
You've got nothing left
to threaten me with.

341
00:33:27.299 --> 00:33:28.842
I'm not afraid of you anymore.

342
00:33:35.307 --> 00:33:36.475
You...

343
00:33:39.102 --> 00:33:40.395
are still afraid.

344
00:33:59.706 --> 00:34:01.375
If you were anyone else in the world...

345
00:34:04.920 --> 00:34:06.630
I'd have killed you a long time ago.

346
00:34:09.632 --> 00:34:13.846
Now. clean up this mess.
and then go get my money.

347
00:34:26.108 --> 00:34:27.775
Armstrong. get up.

348
00:34:27.860 --> 00:34:30.112
Five more.

349
00:34:30.195 --> 00:34:32.364
Yeah. you're gonna wanna hurry
on this one.

350
00:34:32.447 --> 00:34:34.658
What's going on?

351
00:34:34.741 --> 00:34:36.243
You're getting out.

352
00:34:38.954 --> 00:34:40.706
- What?
- You heard me.

353
00:34:41.373 --> 00:34:42.583
On whose authority?

354
00:34:42.666 --> 00:34:46.003
No idea. Warden told me to get you.
so that's what I'm doing.

355
00:34:51.382 --> 00:34:54.719
Hey. You know most guys would kill
to be walking outta here. right?

356
00:34:55.429 --> 00:34:57.431
Oh. yeah. Of course.

357
00:34:59.892 --> 00:35:02.644
I'm just wondering who's waiting for me
on the other side.

358
00:35:02.728 --> 00:35:04.605
Well. there's only one way to find out.

359
00:35:16.450 --> 00:35:17.910
These are yours. Get dressed.

360
00:35:27.628 --> 00:35:29.379
When's the last time
you saw a guy get out of here

361
00:35:29.463 --> 00:35:30.797
with eight years left till parole?

362
00:35:30.881 --> 00:35:31.882
Never.

363
00:35:33.425 --> 00:35:34.676
That's what I figured.

364
00:35:37.012 --> 00:35:39.640
I need you to review the items
and sign at the bottom.

365
00:35:40.349 --> 00:35:43.560
Here's 200 bucks. courtesy of the State.

366
00:35:44.061 --> 00:35:45.771
{\an8}Count it.

367
00:35:47.648 --> 00:35:48.941
That's it?

368
00:35:49.024 --> 00:35:50.025
Cab's waiting.

369
00:36:25.310 --> 00:36:26.311
Where to?

370
00:36:27.729 --> 00:36:29.314
Head west. I'll figure it out.

371
00:36:45.956 --> 00:36:46.957
Dad?

372
00:36:47.583 --> 00:36:48.584
I'm out.

373
00:36:50.586 --> 00:36:52.963
- What?
- <i>I was just discharged.</i>

374
00:36:55.716 --> 00:36:56.884
By who?

375
00:36:57.467 --> 00:37:00.762
I can only think of two possibilities.
and neither one of them bode well for me.

376
00:37:04.224 --> 00:37:06.393
It's Rand. She did it.

377
00:37:07.144 --> 00:37:08.228
<i>How can you be sure?</i>

378
00:37:08.770 --> 00:37:12.649
Because I know her. Dad.
She's using you to smoke me out.

379
00:37:14.276 --> 00:37:16.028
Well. we shouldn't play into her hand.

380
00:37:22.284 --> 00:37:25.120
Rand doesn't hold all the cards.
She just thinks she does.

381
00:37:26.246 --> 00:37:27.456
<i>If you say so.</i>

382
00:37:32.211 --> 00:37:35.714
Go to our place. The high one.
I'll meet you there.

383
00:38:14.711 --> 00:38:15.796
Hey. kid.

384
00:38:19.299 --> 00:38:20.300
Hi. Daddy.

385
00:38:21.552 --> 00:38:23.428
Ooh. Ow. careful.

386
00:38:26.974 --> 00:38:28.809
- Oh.
- Yeah.

387
00:38:32.020 --> 00:38:33.021
I've been better.

388
00:38:41.738 --> 00:38:45.117
You got a plan?

389
00:38:46.493 --> 00:38:47.703
I have the money.

390
00:38:50.289 --> 00:38:51.540
That's my girl.

391
00:38:55.210 --> 00:38:56.753
So. what's the move?

392
00:39:00.424 --> 00:39:02.759
Yeah. you're not gonna like it.

393
00:39:16.190 --> 00:39:18.192
How about here?

394
00:39:19.484 --> 00:39:22.321
Yeah. It seems about right.

395
00:39:29.703 --> 00:39:30.704
You sure about this?

396
00:39:31.872 --> 00:39:33.207
You're asking me this now?

397
00:39:56.688 --> 00:39:57.731
What's up. John?

398
00:40:02.653 --> 00:40:03.987
You're under arrest.

399
00:40:05.697 --> 00:40:06.823
Took you long enough.

400
00:40:10.035 --> 00:40:11.036
Okay.
